      "side": 1,
      "message": "This example runs */20, the same cadence and minute as --regen-heatmap above, so both fire together and double the API load (hosts_range over three months plus all hosts) every 20 minutes. The graphic covers a three-month window, does not need 20-minute freshness, and can be run manually (quads --regen-graph). Suggest a daily off-peak run before business hours but after scheduled assignments go out, staggered off the :00 pileup (move, notify, heatmap and instack all hit :00), for example `17 10 * * *` (10:17 UTC).",
