      "side": 1,
      "message": "This panel chrome hardcodes a light palette (background #f8fafc, text #1f2933, timeline #ffffff, gridlines #e2e8f0). The site themes via data-bs-theme, with a full [data-bs-theme\u003d\"dark\"] block in main.css, so in dark mode this renders as a bright light box on a dark page, unlike every other page (including the heatmap, whose chrome is Bootstrap-themed). The vivid cloud blocks with white text are fine in both themes; only the container, timeline, gridline and text colors need to adapt, for example Bootstrap vars (var(--bs-body-bg), var(--bs-body-color), var(--bs-border-color)) or a [data-bs-theme\u003d\"dark\"] override.",
      "revId": "b47f58fe11cc13d7091d4d428529da73f4eb69fe",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
